Planned:
- router.rs   (from balius-runtime/src/router.rs) — when modules declare typed Watch sets at init-time
- metrics.rs  (from balius-runtime/src/metrics.rs) — when OpenTelemetry surfaces are wired into the host

Removed from the original plan:
- store.rs — Balius's store.rs is a host-side WAL for replay-safe
  worker restart; mitos has a different replay model (dolos's
  archive is the WAL — on restart we re-subscribe via
  `watch_tip(Some(persisted_cursor))` and the chain follower
  re-fetches from there). A focused `CursorStore` in
  `mitos_platform::storage` covers our crash-safety needs in
  ~80 lines instead of vendoring 252 lines of WAL we'd never
  use. See `MITOS_PLATFORM_DEPLOYMENT.md` §"Resolved design
  questions" #7 for the rationale.
